msgid "-s or -l?"
msgstr "-s or -l?"

msgid "<0/> is at home. Now answer <1/> six ways: tap a place."
msgstr "<0/> is at home. Now answer <1/> six ways: tap a place."

msgid "<0/> is the town; <1/> is in Tallinn. Estonian says in with an ending, not a word in front: it puts <2>-s</2> on the end of the name. I live in Tallinn is <3/>"
msgstr "<0/> is the town; <1/> is in Tallinn. Estonian says in with an ending, not a word in front: it puts <2>-s</2> on the end of the name. I live in Tallinn is <3/>"

msgid "2 quizzes"
msgstr "2 quizzes"

msgid "8 minutes"
msgstr "8 minutes"

msgid "A market takes <0>-l</0> by habit: <1/>, at the market. So do names ending in <2>-maa</2>: <3/>, on Saaremaa, and <4/>, in Germany, though English says in there. A few towns and districts take <5>-l</5> as well, such as <6/> and <7/>."
msgstr "A market takes <0>-l</0> by habit: <1/>, at the market. So do names ending in <2>-maa</2>: <3/>, on Saaremaa, and <4/>, in Germany, though English says in there. A few towns and districts take <5>-l</5> as well, such as <6/> and <7/>."

msgid "All of them. You picked the place in every sentence."
msgstr "All of them. You picked the place in every sentence."

msgid "All of them. You picked the right ending every time."
msgstr "All of them. You picked the right ending every time."

